  values (v_part_1, 'Appendix A: 100 Part 1 Practice Questions', 'appendix-a-100-practice-questions', '100 real Part 1 questions across 7 categories, for practice.', '{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Appendix A — Part 1: ১০০টি প্রশ্ন"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"প্রতিটির উত্তর ৩–৪ বাক্যে দাও, রেকর্ড করো। দিনে ১০টি করলে ১০ দিনে পুরো তালিকা শেষ।"}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":3},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Work / Study (১–১০)"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do you work or are you a student?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"What do you like most about your job/studies?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Is there anything you dislike about it?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Why did you choose this field?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do you plan to continue in this area in the future?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"What skills do you need for your work/studies?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do you prefer working alone or in a team?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Is your workplace/university far from your home?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"What would you change about your job/course?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do you think you will still be doing this in ten years?"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":3},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Hometown & Home (১১–২০)"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Where is your hometown?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"What do you like about it?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Has it changed much in recent years?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Would you like to live somewhere else?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"What kind of home do you live in?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Which room do you spend the most time in?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Would you like to change anything about your home?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do you prefer living in a house or a flat?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Is your neighbourhood a good place for children?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"What is the most popular place in your hometown for visitors?"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":3},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Daily Life & Free Time (২১–৪০)"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"What do you usually do at weekends?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"How do you usually spend your evenings?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Are you a morning person or a night person?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do you have a busy daily routine?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"What do you do to relax?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do you prefer indoor or outdoor activities?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"How often do you meet your friends?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do you enjoy shopping?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"How do you usually travel around your city?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do you like cooking?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"What kind of food do you enjoy most?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do you often eat at restaurants?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"How much sleep do you usually get?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do you do any exercise?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"What kind of music do you listen to?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do you enjoy reading?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do you watch films or TV series?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do you play any sports?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do you have any hobbies you have had since childhood?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"How do you usually celebrate your birthday?"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":3},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Technology & Media (৪১–৫৫)"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"How often do you use your mobile phone?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"What do you mostly use the internet for?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do you use social media?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Has technology changed the way you study or work?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do you prefer texting or calling?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do you take a lot of photographs?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"How do you usually get your news?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do you think people spend too much time on screens?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"What was your first mobile phone like?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do you shop online?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do you play video games?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do you use apps to learn anything?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"How would your life change without the internet?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do you prefer reading on paper or on a screen?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do you listen to podcasts or audiobooks?"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":3},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"People & Relationships (৫৬–৭০)"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do you have a large family?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Who are you closest to in your family?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do you spend much time with your relatives?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"How do you usually keep in touch with friends?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do you prefer a few close friends or many acquaintances?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"What makes someone a good friend?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do you enjoy meeting new people?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Have you known your best friend for a long time?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do you and your friends have similar interests?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do you often help other people?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Are neighbours important in your country?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do you know your neighbours well?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do children in your country spend a lot of time with grandparents?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do you prefer spending time alone or with others?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"How do people usually make friends in your country?"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":3},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Environment, Weather & Places (৭১–৮৫)"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"What is the weather usually like in your country?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"What is your favourite season?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Does the weather affect your mood?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do you prefer hot or cold weather?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Are there many parks near your home?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do you like spending time in nature?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Is air pollution a problem where you live?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do people in your country recycle?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Have you ever been to the countryside?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do you like going to the beach?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"What is the most beautiful place you have visited?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do you enjoy travelling?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"How do you usually plan a trip?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Would you like to visit another country?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do you prefer short trips or long holidays?"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":3},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Miscellaneous (৮৬–১০০)"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do you like giving gifts?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"What kind of clothes do you usually wear?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do you follow fashion?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Are you good at remembering things?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do you make lists?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"How do you usually manage your time?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do you like surprises?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Are you a patient person?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do you often lose things?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do you enjoy learning new languages?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"What was your favourite subject at school?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do you prefer to plan or be spontaneous?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"How do you feel about public transport?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do you like being in crowded places?"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"What do you hope to do in the next five years?"}]}]}]}]}'::jsonb, 'published', 'advanced', 20, now());

  -- Part 2 Masterclass: Rules & Technique
  insert into lessons (node_id, title, slug, excerpt, content, status, difficulty, estimated_minutes, published_at)
  values (v_part_2, 'Part 2 Masterclass: Rules & Technique', 'part-2-masterclass', 'How Part 2 works, a one-minute note-taking framework, and a structure for filling the full two minutes.', '{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"অধ্যায় ১৭ — Part 2 (Cue Card) Masterclass"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"অধিকাংশ শিক্ষার্থীর সবচেয়ে ভয়ের অংশ। কিন্তু এটিই আসলে সবচেয়ে নিয়ন্ত্রণযোগ্য — কারণ এখানে কেউ তোমাকে বাধা দেয় না, প্রশ্ন বদলায় না, এবং প্রস্তুতির জন্য এক মিনিট সময় দেওয়া হয়।"}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":3},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"১৭.১ কীভাবে কাজ করে"}]},{"type":"table","content":[{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableHeader","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"ধাপ"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"সময়"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"কী হয়"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"কার্ড দেওয়া"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"—"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"একটি বিষয় + সাধারণত ৩–৪টি bullet point"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"প্রস্তুতি"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"১ মিনিট"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"কাগজ ও পেন্সিল দেওয়া হয় — নোট নেওয়া বাধ্যতামূলক নয়, কিন্তু নেবে"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"বলা"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"১–২ মিনিট"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"একটানা; examiner বাধা দেবেন না"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Follow-up"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"~২০ সেকেন্ড"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"১–২টি ছোট প্রশ্ন"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"callout","attrs":{"variant":"note"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"দুটি মারাত্মক ভুল ❌ ১ মিনিটের আগে থেমে যাওয়া। Examiner \"Thank you\" বলার আগে থামলে FC-তে সরাসরি ক্ষতি। লক্ষ্য: examiner তোমাকে থামান, তুমি নিজে থেমো না। ❌ নোটে সম্পূর্ণ বাক্য লেখা। ১ মিনিটে বাক্য লেখা সম্ভব নয়, আর লিখলে তুমি পড়তে শুরু করবে — যা সাথে সাথে ধরা পড়ে। শুধু কীওয়ার্ড।"}]}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":3},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"১৭.২ ১ মিনিটের নোট-সূত্র"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Bullet point-গুলো মনে রাখার জন্য নয় — সেগুলো কার্ডেই লেখা আছে, তুমি বলার সময় দেখতে পারবে। নোটে শুধু কীওয়ার্ড লেখো, প্রতিটি bullet-এর জন্য ২–৩টি।"}]},{"type":"callout","attrs":{"variant":"note"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"নোটের সঠিক চেহারা Cue card: Describe a person who has influenced you.  ১ মিনিটে যা লিখবে (কীওয়ার্ড মাত্র): WHO → uncle Kamal, mechanic, Khulna HOW MET → childhood summers, his workshop WHAT DID → taught me to fix things, patience, never shouted WHY INFLUENCE → problem-solving mindset, chose engineering because of him EXTRA → died 2021, still hear his voice when stuck"}]}]},{"type":"callout","attrs":{"variant":"note"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"একটি গোপন কৌশল নোটে একটি \"EXTRA\" লাইন সবসময় রাখো — একটি আবেগ, একটি ছোট গল্প, বা একটি বর্তমান সংযোগ। সময় ফুরিয়ে যাওয়ার আগেই bullet শেষ হয়ে গেলে এই লাইনটাই তোমাকে বাকি ৩০ সেকেন্ড টেনে নিয়ে যাবে। Part 2-এ সময় ফুরিয়ে যাওয়ার ভয় দূর করার সবচেয়ে কার্যকর উপায় এটি।"}]}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":3},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"১৭.৩ সময় ভরাট করার কাঠামো"}]},{"type":"table","content":[{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableHeader","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"পর্যায়"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"সময়"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"কী বলবে"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"শুরু"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"~১০ সেকেন্ড"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"বিষয় ঘোষণা + একটি ব্যক্তিগত সংযোগ (\"The person I''d like to talk about is...\")"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"প্রতিটি bullet"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"~২৫ সেকেন্ড"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"প্রতিটিতে একটি নির্দিষ্ট বিবরণ বা ছোট ঘটনা"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"শেষ bullet (\"why/how you felt\")"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"~৩০ সেকেন্ড"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"এখানেই সবচেয়ে বেশি সময় দাও — এটিই সবচেয়ে খোলা প্রশ্ন"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"সমাপ্তি"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"~১৫ সেকেন্ড"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"বর্তমানের সাথে সংযোগ (\"Even now, whenever I...\")"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":3},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"১৭.৪ চারটি সম্পূর্ণ Model Answer"}]}]}'::jsonb, 'published', 'advanced', 10, now());

  -- Part 2 Model Answer: A Person Who Influenced You
  insert into lessons (node_id, title, slug, excerpt, content, status, difficulty, estimated_minutes, published_at)
  values (v_part_2, 'Part 2 Model Answer: A Person Who Influenced You', 'model-answer-person-who-influenced-you', 'A full Band 8 cue-card answer, with a criterion-by-criterion breakdown of why it works.', '{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":4},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Cue Card 1 — Describe a person who has influenced you"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You should say: who this person is · how you know them · what they have done · and explain why they have influenced you."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"pronounce","attrs":{"text":"The person I''d like to talk about is my uncle Kamal, my father''s younger brother. He passed away a couple of years ago, but he''s probably still the single biggest influence on how I think about things.  He ran a small motorcycle repair workshop in Khulna, and as a child I spent almost every summer holiday there. My parents would send me off for a month and I''d basically live in that workshop — handing him spanners, sweeping up, getting oil all over my clothes. I think I was about eight when it started.  What he did, without ever really announcing it, was teach me how to think through a problem. He''d never just fix something in front of me. He''d hand me the part and say, \"Right, what do you reckon is wrong with it?\" And then he''d wait. Sometimes for ten minutes. He had this extraordinary patience — I never once heard him raise his voice, at me or at a customer, and believe me, some of those customers deserved it.  The reason he influenced me so much is that he completely changed what I thought intelligence was. Before that I assumed clever people were the ones who got good marks. He''d barely finished school, but he could listen to an engine for thirty seconds and tell you what was wrong with it. That stuck with me. I ended up choosing engineering at university largely because of those summers, and honestly, whenever I''m stuck on something difficult at work, I still catch myself hearing his voice saying, \"So what do you reckon?\"","label":"🔊 Listen to this answer"}}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Band 8 — প্রায় ২ মিনিট The person I''d like to talk about is my uncle Kamal, my father''s younger brother. He passed away a couple of years ago, but he''s probably still the single biggest influence on how I think about things.  He ran a small motorcycle repair workshop in Khulna, and as a child I spent almost every summer holiday there. My parents would send me off for a month and I''d basically live in that workshop — handing him spanners, sweeping up, getting oil all over my clothes. I think I was about eight when it started.  What he did, without ever really announcing it, was teach me how to think through a problem. He''d never just fix something in front of me. He''d hand me the part and say, \"Right, what do you reckon is wrong with it?\" And then he''d wait. Sometimes for ten minutes. He had this extraordinary patience — I never once heard him raise his voice, at me or at a customer, and believe me, some of those customers deserved it.  The reason he influenced me so much is that he completely changed what I thought intelligence was. Before that I assumed clever people were the ones who got good marks. He''d barely finished school, but he could listen to an engine for thirty seconds and tell you what was wrong with it. That stuck with me. I ended up choosing engineering at university largely because of those summers, and honestly, whenever I''m stuck on something difficult at work, I still catch myself hearing his voice saying, \"So what do you reckon?\""}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":4},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"কেন এটা Band 8"}]},{"type":"table","content":[{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableHeader","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Criterion"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"কী কাজ করেছে"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fluency & Coherence"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"পুরো ২ মিনিট ভরাট; চারটি bullet ক্রমানুসারে; স্বাভাবিক কথ্য সংযোগ (What he did..., The reason he influenced me..., That stuck with me)।"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Lexical Resource"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Idiomatic ও স্বাভাবিক: basically live in that workshop, stuck with me, catch myself, extraordinary patience, deserved it। কোনো জোর করে বসানো কঠিন শব্দ নেই।"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Grammar"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"would (past habit), past continuous, present perfect, reported speech, cleft (What he did... was teach me), relative clause — সব স্বাভাবিকভাবে।"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"বিষয়বস্তু"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"নির্দিষ্ট বিবরণ (spanners, আট বছর বয়স, ত্রিশ সেকেন্ড) গল্পটিকে বিশ্বাসযোগ্য করে। হাস্যরস ও আবেগ ব্যক্তিত্ব যোগ করে।"}]}]}]}]}]}'::jsonb, 'published', 'advanced', 8, now());

  -- Part 2 Model Answer: A Place You Like to Visit
  insert into lessons (node_id, title, slug, excerpt, content, status, difficulty, estimated_minutes, published_at)
  values (v_part_2, 'Part 2 Model Answer: A Place You Like to Visit', 'model-answer-place-you-like-to-visit', 'A full Band 8 cue-card answer about an ordinary place, and why that''s exactly the point.', '{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":4},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Cue Card 2 — Describe a place you like to visit"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You should say: where it is · how often you go · what you do there · and explain why you like it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"pronounce","attrs":{"text":"I''d like to talk about a rooftop café near my office in Dhanmondi. It''s nothing fancy at all — about eight tables, plastic chairs, a fairly tired-looking awning — but it''s become my favourite spot in the city.  It''s on the fifth floor of an old building, and you have to go up a staircase that honestly doesn''t inspire much confidence. But once you get to the top, you''re above the noise. That''s the whole appeal, really. Dhaka is relentless at street level, and up there you can actually hear yourself think.  I go maybe twice a week, usually on my way home. What I do there is fairly unexciting — I order a cup of tea, sometimes a plate of shingara, and I just sit. Occasionally I read, but more often I end up watching the traffic below and doing absolutely nothing productive, which I''ve come to realise is the point.  The reason I like it so much is that it''s the only place in my routine where nobody expects anything from me. At home there''s family, at work there''s deadlines. That rooftop is about forty minutes where my phone stays in my pocket. I discovered it completely by accident about two years ago — I was sheltering from the rain — and I''ve been going ever since. I''d be genuinely upset if it closed down.","label":"🔊 Listen to this answer"}}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Band 8 — প্রায় ২ মিনিট I''d like to talk about a rooftop café near my office in Dhanmondi. It''s nothing fancy at all — about eight tables, plastic chairs, a fairly tired-looking awning — but it''s become my favourite spot in the city.  It''s on the fifth floor of an old building, and you have to go up a staircase that honestly doesn''t inspire much confidence. But once you get to the top, you''re above the noise. That''s the whole appeal, really. Dhaka is relentless at street level, and up there you can actually hear yourself think.  I go maybe twice a week, usually on my way home. What I do there is fairly unexciting — I order a cup of tea, sometimes a plate of shingara, and I just sit. Occasionally I read, but more often I end up watching the traffic below and doing absolutely nothing productive, which I''ve come to realise is the point.  The reason I like it so much is that it''s the only place in my routine where nobody expects anything from me. At home there''s family, at work there''s deadlines. That rooftop is about forty minutes where my phone stays in my pocket. I discovered it completely by accident about two years ago — I was sheltering from the rain — and I''ve been going ever since. I''d be genuinely upset if it closed down."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"লক্ষ করো: বিষয়টি অসাধারণ কিছু নয় — একটি সাধারণ চায়ের দোকান। Band 8 আসে বিষয়ের অসাধারণত্ব থেকে নয়, বর্ণনার নির্দিষ্টতা ও স্বাভাবিকতা থেকে।"}]}]}'::jsonb, 'published', 'advanced', 6, now());

  -- Part 2 Model Answer: A Difficult Decision You Made
  insert into lessons (node_id, title, slug, excerpt, content, status, difficulty, estimated_minutes, published_at)
  values (v_part_2, 'Part 2 Model Answer: A Difficult Decision You Made', 'model-answer-difficult-decision', 'A full Band 8 cue-card answer that shows nuance rather than a one-sided view.', '{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":4},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Cue Card 3 — Describe a difficult decision you made"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You should say: what the decision was · when you made it · what made it difficult · and explain how you feel about it now."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"pronounce","attrs":{"text":"The decision I want to talk about is turning down a job offer abroad, which happened about eighteen months ago.  A company in Dubai offered me a role that paid roughly three times what I was earning here. On paper it was a no-brainer. My colleagues certainly thought so — a couple of them told me outright that I''d be mad to refuse it.  What made it so difficult was that my father had been diagnosed with a heart condition about two months earlier. He was recovering well, and he insisted, repeatedly, that I should go. But I kept thinking about what would happen if something went wrong and I was five hours away by plane. So I was caught between a genuinely life-changing opportunity and a fear I couldn''t really justify with logic. I went back and forth for nearly three weeks, which is completely unlike me — I''m normally quite decisive.  In the end I turned it down, and to be honest, I still have mixed feelings about it. Financially it was clearly the wrong call. There are months when I look at my salary and wince a bit. But my father had a second scare last winter, and I was at the hospital within twenty minutes. I don''t think I''d have forgiven myself if I''d been abroad. So I suppose the honest answer is that I don''t regret it, but I haven''t entirely made peace with it either.","label":"🔊 Listen to this answer"}}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Band 8 — প্রায় ২ মিনিট The decision I want to talk about is turning down a job offer abroad, which happened about eighteen months ago.  A company in Dubai offered me a role that paid roughly three times what I was earning here. On paper it was a no-brainer. My colleagues certainly thought so — a couple of them told me outright that I''d be mad to refuse it.  What made it so difficult was that my father had been diagnosed with a heart condition about two months earlier. He was recovering well, and he insisted, repeatedly, that I should go. But I kept thinking about what would happen if something went wrong and I was five hours away by plane. So I was caught between a genuinely life-changing opportunity and a fear I couldn''t really justify with logic. I went back and forth for nearly three weeks, which is completely unlike me — I''m normally quite decisive.  In the end I turned it down, and to be honest, I still have mixed feelings about it. Financially it was clearly the wrong call. There are months when I look at my salary and wince a bit. But my father had a second scare last winter, and I was at the hospital within twenty minutes. I don''t think I''d have forgiven myself if I''d been abroad. So I suppose the honest answer is that I don''t regret it, but I haven''t entirely made peace with it either."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"লক্ষ করো: শেষে nuance — \"I don''t regret it, but I haven''t entirely made peace with it either\"। একপেশে সিদ্ধান্ত না দিয়ে জটিলতা স্বীকার করা Band 8-এর অন্যতম স্পষ্ট চিহ্ন।"}]}]}'::jsonb, 'published', 'advanced', 6, now());

  -- Part 2 Model Answer: Something Useful You Learned
  insert into lessons (node_id, title, slug, excerpt, content, status, difficulty, estimated_minutes, published_at)
  values (v_part_2, 'Part 2 Model Answer: Something Useful You Learned', 'model-answer-something-useful-learned', 'A full Band 8 cue-card answer, plus three ways to keep talking if you finish early.', '{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":4},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Cue Card 4 — Describe something you learned that was useful"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You should say: what it was · how you learned it · how long it took · and explain why it has been useful."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"pronounce","attrs":{"text":"The thing I''d like to talk about is learning to drive, which I picked up embarrassingly late — I was twenty-eight.  I''d put it off for years, partly because public transport was good enough where I lived, and partly, if I''m honest, because I was nervous about it. Dhaka traffic is not a forgiving place to learn. What finally pushed me was a new job that involved travelling to sites outside the city, where there was simply no other way of getting around.  I learned with an instructor from a small driving school — a very calm man in his sixties who had clearly seen every possible mistake before. It took about three months of twice-weekly lessons, which is longer than most people need, but I wasn''t in any rush and I wanted to feel genuinely confident rather than just pass the test.  It''s turned out to be far more useful than I expected. The obvious benefit is the job — I can get to a site an hour away without spending half a day on buses. But the bigger thing has been the independence. I can take my parents to hospital appointments, I can drive out of the city at the weekend, and I''m no longer dependent on other people''s schedules. And there was something else I didn''t anticipate: proving to myself that I could learn something that intimidated me. That gave me the confidence to take on a few other things I''d been avoiding.","label":"🔊 Listen to this answer"}}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Band 8 — প্রায় ২ মিনিট The thing I''d like to talk about is learning to drive, which I picked up embarrassingly late — I was twenty-eight.  I''d put it off for years, partly because public transport was good enough where I lived, and partly, if I''m honest, because I was nervous about it. Dhaka traffic is not a forgiving place to learn. What finally pushed me was a new job that involved travelling to sites outside the city, where there was simply no other way of getting around.  I learned with an instructor from a small driving school — a very calm man in his sixties who had clearly seen every possible mistake before. It took about three months of twice-weekly lessons, which is longer than most people need, but I wasn''t in any rush and I wanted to feel genuinely confident rather than just pass the test.  It''s turned out to be far more useful than I expected. The obvious benefit is the job — I can get to a site an hour away without spending half a day on buses. But the bigger thing has been the independence. I can take my parents to hospital appointments, I can drive out of the city at the weekend, and I''m no longer dependent on other people''s schedules. And there was something else I didn''t anticipate: proving to myself that I could learn something that intimidated me. That gave me the confidence to take on a few other things I''d been avoiding."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":3},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"১৭.৫ Part 2-এ সময় ফুরিয়ে গেলে"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"যদি সব bullet শেষ হয়ে যায় কিন্তু examiner এখনো থামাননি, এই তিনটি পথ খোলা:"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"বর্তমানের সাথে সংযোগ: \"Even now, whenever I...\" / \"It''s actually still part of my routine...\""}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"অন্য কারো দৃষ্টিভঙ্গি: \"My brother had a completely different experience with this, actually...\""}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"ভবিষ্যৎ: \"I''m hoping to go back next year, in fact...\""}]}]}]}]}'::jsonb, 'published', 'advanced', 8, now());

  -- Appendix B: 40 Cue Cards for Practice
  insert into lessons (node_id, title, slug, excerpt, content, status, difficulty, estimated_minutes, published_at)
  values (v_part_2, 'Appendix B: 40 Cue Cards for Practice', 'appendix-b-40-cue-cards', '40 real Part 2 cue cards across 5 categories, for practice.', '{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Appendix B — Part 2: ৪০টি Cue Card"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"প্রতিটির জন্য ১ মিনিট নোট + ২ মিনিট বলা। ঘড়ি ছাড়া অনুশীলন কোরো না।"}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":3},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"People (১–৮)"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Describe a person who has influenced you."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Describe an old person you admire."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Describe a friend you have known for a long time."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Describe a person who is good at their job."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Describe someone who helped you when you had a problem."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Describe a family member you spend a lot of time with."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Describe a person you would like to meet."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Describe a teacher you remember well."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":3},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Places (৯–১৬)"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Describe a place you like to visit in your free time."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Describe a city you have visited and enjoyed."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Describe a quiet place you go to."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Describe a building you find interesting."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Describe a shop or market you like."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Describe a place in your country you would recommend to a visitor."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Describe a park or garden you have been to."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Describe a place where you studied."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":3},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Objects (১৭–২৪)"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Describe something you own that is important to you."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Describe a gift you received that you liked."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Describe a piece of technology you use often."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Describe an item of clothing you wear a lot."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Describe something you bought recently."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Describe a book that had an effect on you."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Describe a photograph you like."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Describe something you would like to buy in the future."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":3},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Events & Experiences (২৫–৩২)"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Describe a time when you learned something new."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Describe a journey you remember well."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Describe an occasion when you helped someone."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Describe a time when you were very busy."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Describe a celebration you took part in."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Describe a time you had to make a difficult decision."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Describe an occasion when you were late."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Describe a time when you received good news."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":3},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Abstract & Preferences (৩৩–৪০)"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Describe a skill you would like to learn."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Describe a change you would like to make in your life."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Describe a habit you would like to give up."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Describe an ambition you have not achieved yet."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Describe a website or app you find useful."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Describe a rule you disagree with."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Describe a subject you would like to study in the future."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Describe an advertisement you remember."}]}]}]}]}'::jsonb, 'published', 'advanced', 15, now());

  -- Part 3 Masterclass: Rules & Technique
  insert into lessons (node_id, title, slug, excerpt, content, status, difficulty, estimated_minutes, published_at)
  values (v_part_3, 'Part 3 Masterclass: Rules & Technique', 'part-3-masterclass', 'Five rules for Part 3, and the language of opinion, speculation, and generalisation you''ll need.', '{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"অধ্যায় ১৮ — Part 3 Masterclass"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Part 3-ই সেই জায়গা যেখানে Band 7 আর Band 8-এর পার্থক্য তৈরি হয়। এখানে প্রশ্ন ব্যক্তিগত নয় — সমাজ, প্রবণতা, ভবিষ্যৎ, কারণ ও ফলাফল নিয়ে। Examiner তোমার চিন্তা করার ক্ষমতা ইংরেজিতে দেখতে চান।"}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":3},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"১৮.১ Part 3-এর পাঁচটি নিয়ম"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"৪–৬ বাক্য — Part 1-এর চেয়ে লম্বা।"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"আমি\" থেকে \"মানুষ\"-এ যাও। ব্যক্তিগত উদাহরণ দেওয়া যায়, কিন্তু উত্তরটি সাধারণ প্রবণতা নিয়ে হতে হবে।"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"সরাসরি উত্তর → কারণ → উদাহরণ → শর্ত/বিপরীত দিক। এটাই কাঠামো।"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"অনুমানের ভাষা ব্যবহার করো — এখানে নিশ্চিত হওয়ার দরকার নেই: I''d imagine, it may well be that, presumably।"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"I don''t know\" বলে থেমো না। না জানলেও একটি যুক্তি দাঁড় করাও: \"I''m not entirely sure, but my guess would be that...\""}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":3},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"১৮.২ Part 3-এর ভাষার ভাণ্ডার"}]},{"type":"table","content":[{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableHeader","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"কাজ"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"ভাষা"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"মতামত"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I''d say... • My sense is that... • If you ask me... • I''d be inclined to think that..."}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"অনুমান"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I''d imagine... • It may well be that... • Presumably... • My guess would be that..."}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"সাধারণীকরণ"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"By and large... • As a rule... • More often than not... • Generally speaking..."}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"শর্ত দেওয়া"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"It depends largely on... • Up to a point... • That said... • To some extent, yes, but..."}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"তুলনা (সময়)"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Compared with a generation ago... • Things have shifted quite dramatically since..."}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"কারণ"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A lot of it comes down to... • It stems partly from... • The root of it is probably..."}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"ভবিষ্যৎ"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I suspect we''ll see... • It''s likely to... • I wouldn''t be surprised if..."}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"দ্বিমত"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I''m not sure I''d go that far. • I can see the argument, but... • That''s true up to a point, though..."}]}]}]}]}]}'::jsonb, 'published', 'advanced', 10, now());

  -- Part 3 Model Answers: Influence & Role Models
  insert into lessons (node_id, title, slug, excerpt, content, status, difficulty, estimated_minutes, published_at)
  values (v_part_3, 'Part 3 Model Answers: Influence & Role Models', 'model-answers-influence-role-models', 'Band 8 model answers on influence and role models.', '{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":4},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"টপিক: Influence & Role Models"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Q: Do you think celebrities make good role models for young people?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"pronounce","attrs":{"text":"Generally, no — though not because celebrities are bad people. It''s more that what young people see is a heavily edited version of someone''s life, so they end up comparing their own ordinary reality with someone else''s highlight reel. That''s a losing game. I''d say the more useful role models tend to be people you actually know — a teacher, an older cousin — because you see their failures as well as their successes. The one exception might be celebrities who are genuinely open about their struggles, but those are fairly rare.","label":"🔊 Listen to this answer"}}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Generally, no — though not because celebrities are bad people. It''s more that what young people see is a heavily edited version of someone''s life, so they end up comparing their own ordinary reality with someone else''s highlight reel. That''s a losing game. I''d say the more useful role models tend to be people you actually know — a teacher, an older cousin — because you see their failures as well as their successes. The one exception might be celebrities who are genuinely open about their struggles, but those are fairly rare."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"কেন এটা কাজ করে: সরাসরি অবস্থান → কারণ → বিকল্প → ব্যতিক্রম স্বীকার (nuance)। a losing game, highlight reel — স্বাভাবিক idiomatic ভাষা।"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Q: How has the role of parents changed in recent years?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"pronounce","attrs":{"text":"Quite substantially, I think. A generation ago, at least here, parenting was fairly directive — parents decided what you studied, often who you married, and children were expected to fall in line. Now it''s much more of a negotiation. Part of that comes down to education, I''d imagine, and part of it is simply that young people have far more information and far more options than their parents did. Whether that''s entirely a good thing is debatable, actually — some of my friends'' parents seem almost afraid to set any boundaries at all.","label":"🔊 Listen to this answer"}}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Quite substantially, I think. A generation ago, at least here, parenting was fairly directive — parents decided what you studied, often who you married, and children were expected to fall in line. Now it''s much more of a negotiation. Part of that comes down to education, I''d imagine, and part of it is simply that young people have far more information and far more options than their parents did. Whether that''s entirely a good thing is debatable, actually — some of my friends'' parents seem almost afraid to set any boundaries at all."}]}]}'::jsonb, 'published', 'advanced', 8, now());

  -- Part 3 Model Answers: Places & Cities
  insert into lessons (node_id, title, slug, excerpt, content, status, difficulty, estimated_minutes, published_at)
  values (v_part_3, 'Part 3 Model Answers: Places & Cities', 'model-answers-places-cities', 'Band 8 model answers on places and cities.', '{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":4},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"টপিক: Places & Cities"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Q: Why do you think so many people are moving to cities?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"pronounce","attrs":{"text":"It really comes down to opportunity, in most cases. Jobs, universities, hospitals — they''re all concentrated in a handful of cities, so if you want any of those things you more or less have to move. There''s also a social dimension people don''t talk about much: once your friends and cousins have all left, staying behind starts to feel like being left out. I suspect that pull is almost as strong as the economic one, particularly for younger people.","label":"🔊 Listen to this answer"}}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"It really comes down to opportunity, in most cases. Jobs, universities, hospitals — they''re all concentrated in a handful of cities, so if you want any of those things you more or less have to move. There''s also a social dimension people don''t talk about much: once your friends and cousins have all left, staying behind starts to feel like being left out. I suspect that pull is almost as strong as the economic one, particularly for younger people."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Q: What could governments do to make cities more liveable?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"pronounce","attrs":{"text":"The single biggest thing would be to take public space seriously. In most fast-growing cities, parks and pavements are the first things sacrificed when land gets expensive, and that has a real effect on how people live — you end up with a city where the only place to spend time is a shopping mall. Beyond that, I''d prioritise mass transit over roads, because widening roads just fills them up again. None of this is technically difficult; it''s more that the benefits take fifteen years to show and elections come round every five.","label":"🔊 Listen to this answer"}}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The single biggest thing would be to take public space seriously. In most fast-growing cities, parks and pavements are the first things sacrificed when land gets expensive, and that has a real effect on how people live — you end up with a city where the only place to spend time is a shopping mall. Beyond that, I''d prioritise mass transit over roads, because widening roads just fills them up again. None of this is technically difficult; it''s more that the benefits take fifteen years to show and elections come round every five."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"কেন এটা কাজ করে: শেষ বাক্যটি Band 8-এর চিহ্ন — রাজনৈতিক বাস্তবতা সম্পর্কে সচেতনতা, শুধু আদর্শ সমাধান নয়।"}]}]}'::jsonb, 'published', 'advanced', 8, now());

  -- Part 3 Model Answers: Decisions & Risk
  insert into lessons (node_id, title, slug, excerpt, content, status, difficulty, estimated_minutes, published_at)
  values (v_part_3, 'Part 3 Model Answers: Decisions & Risk', 'model-answers-decisions-risk', 'Band 8 model answers on decisions and risk.', '{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":4},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"টপিক: Decisions & Risk"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Q: Are young people today better at making decisions than previous generations?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"pronounce","attrs":{"text":"I''d say they''re better informed but not necessarily better at deciding. They can research anything in seconds, which their parents couldn''t, but I think that abundance creates its own problem — when there are forty options, committing to one feels like a loss. A friend of mine spent six months choosing a master''s programme and ended up more anxious at the end than at the start. So more information, yes; more clarity, I''m not so sure.","label":"🔊 Listen to this answer"}}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I''d say they''re better informed but not necessarily better at deciding. They can research anything in seconds, which their parents couldn''t, but I think that abundance creates its own problem — when there are forty options, committing to one feels like a loss. A friend of mine spent six months choosing a master''s programme and ended up more anxious at the end than at the start. So more information, yes; more clarity, I''m not so sure."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Q: Should important decisions be made by individuals or by groups?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"pronounce","attrs":{"text":"It depends enormously on the type of decision. For anything where the consequences fall on one person — career, marriage — I''d say the individual has to decide, even if they get it wrong, because living with someone else''s choice tends to breed resentment. For decisions affecting a lot of people, though, groups are usually better, mainly because they catch each other''s blind spots. The risk with groups is that they drift towards whatever''s least objectionable rather than what''s actually best.","label":"🔊 Listen to this answer"}}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"It depends enormously on the type of decision. For anything where the consequences fall on one person — career, marriage — I''d say the individual has to decide, even if they get it wrong, because living with someone else''s choice tends to breed resentment. For decisions affecting a lot of people, though, groups are usually better, mainly because they catch each other''s blind spots. The risk with groups is that they drift towards whatever''s least objectionable rather than what''s actually best."}]}]}'::jsonb, 'published', 'advanced', 6, now());

  -- Part 3 Model Answers: Learning & Skills
  insert into lessons (node_id, title, slug, excerpt, content, status, difficulty, estimated_minutes, published_at)
  values (v_part_3, 'Part 3 Model Answers: Learning & Skills', 'model-answers-learning-skills', 'Band 8 model answers on learning and skills, plus how to disagree politely in Part 3.', '{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":4},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"টপিক: Learning & Skills"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Q: Do you think practical skills are as valued as academic qualifications?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"pronounce","attrs":{"text":"Not nearly as much as they should be, at least in this part of the world. There''s still enormous social pressure to get a degree, almost regardless of whether it leads anywhere, while skilled trades are looked down on despite often paying better. I think that''s slowly changing as graduate unemployment becomes more visible, but attitudes like that shift over decades rather than years. Realistically, most parents I know would still rather see their child in a low-paid office job than running a successful workshop.","label":"🔊 Listen to this answer"}}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Not nearly as much as they should be, at least in this part of the world. There''s still enormous social pressure to get a degree, almost regardless of whether it leads anywhere, while skilled trades are looked down on despite often paying better. I think that''s slowly changing as graduate unemployment becomes more visible, but attitudes like that shift over decades rather than years. Realistically, most parents I know would still rather see their child in a low-paid office job than running a successful workshop."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Q: How might the skills people need change in the next twenty years?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"pronounce","attrs":{"text":"I''d imagine the technical specifics will change faster than anyone can predict, so the skill that really matters will be the ability to keep retraining. My father did essentially the same job for thirty-five years; I''d be astonished if I did the same. Beyond that, I suspect the things machines are worst at will become more valuable — judgement, persuading people, handling situations with no clear right answer. Whether education systems can adapt quickly enough is another question entirely.","label":"🔊 Listen to this answer"}}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I''d imagine the technical specifics will change faster than anyone can predict, so the skill that really matters will be the ability to keep retraining. My father did essentially the same job for thirty-five years; I''d be astonished if I did the same. Beyond that, I suspect the things machines are worst at will become more valuable — judgement, persuading people, handling situations with no clear right answer. Whether education systems can adapt quickly enough is another question entirely."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":3},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"১৮.৪ Part 3-এ দ্বিমত করা"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Examiner মাঝে মাঝে তোমার মতের বিরুদ্ধে যাবেন (\"But don''t you think...?\")। এটি ফাঁদ নয় — এটি সুযোগ। তিনি দেখতে চান তুমি নিজের অবস্থান রক্ষা করতে পারো কিনা।"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"pronounce","attrs":{"text":"Examiner: But surely technology has made people less social?  ✅ Band 8 উত্তর: \"I can see why people say that, and I''d agree it''s changed the *shape* of socialising. But less social? I''m not sure I''d go that far. My mother speaks to her sisters in three different countries almost daily, which would have been unthinkable and unaffordable twenty years ago. What''s probably true is that we have more contact but less depth — and that''s a real loss. So I''d put it differently: not less social, but socialising differently, with some genuine costs.\"","label":"🔊 Listen to this answer"}}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"দ্বিমত করার সঠিক পদ্ধতি Examiner: But surely technology has made people less social?  ✅ Band 8 উত্তর: \"I can see why people say that, and I''d agree it''s changed the *shape* of socialising. But less social? I''m not sure I''d go that far. My mother speaks to her sisters in three different countries almost daily, which would have been unthinkable and unaffordable twenty years ago. What''s probably true is that we have more contact but less depth — and that''s a real loss. So I''d put it differently: not less social, but socialising differently, with some genuine costs.\""}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"কাঠামো: স্বীকার করো → আংশিক একমত হও → নিজের অবস্থান স্পষ্ট করো → পুনর্গঠন করো। কখনো সরাসরি \"No, you are wrong\" বোলো না, আবার নিজের মত পুরোপুরি ছেড়েও দিও না।"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"কৌশল ও অনুশীলন"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"পরীক্ষার দিন, একা অনুশীলনের পদ্ধতি, এবং নিজের মূল্যায়ন"}]}]}'::jsonb, 'published', 'advanced', 10, now());

